name atomic-2020-tuples
# ATOMIC 2020: a tuple on every line, three fields parted by tabs, no header row. The set's README:
#   "- each line represents a distinct commonsense tuple"
#   "- column 1: head node/concept"  "- column 2: edge relation (e.g., xWant,xAttr,AtLocation)"  "- column 3: tail node/concept"
# A field that holds a quote or a tab is written between double quotes, a quote in it doubled.
# Each row is the claim of its head, its relation and its tail, every one as written.
match train.tsv dev.tsv test.tsv

tier row by \n
names head relation tail
quoted
tier field by \t

thing row head
content head relation tail
# the relation column is ATOMIC's own relation inventory (README: "edge relation (e.g., xWant, xAttr, AtLocation)")
value - relation
relate row relation to tail
